# Deep Learning Image Classification using CNN

## 📌 Overview

This project implements a Convolutional Neural Network (CNN) using TensorFlow to classify images from the Fashion MNIST dataset. The model is trained to recognize 10 different categories of clothing items.

## 🎯 Objective

To build and train a deep learning model for image classification and visualize its performance using accuracy graphs and predictions.

## 🛠 Technologies Used

- Python
- TensorFlow / Keras
- NumPy
- Matplotlib

## 📂 Dataset

Fashion MNIST Dataset:
- 60,000 training images
- 10,000 testing images
- 10 clothing categories
- Image size: 28×28 pixels

## 🧠 Model Architecture

- Conv2D Layer
- MaxPooling Layer
- Conv2D Layer
- Flatten Layer
- Dense Layer
- Output Layer (Softmax)

## 🚀 How to Run

1. Install dependencies:

```bash
pip install tensorflow matplotlib numpy
```

2. Run the project:

```bash
python main.py
```

## 📊 Results

- Achieved approximately **90% test accuracy**
- Generated training and validation accuracy graphs
- Displayed sample predictions on test images

